// The numbers skip 5, 8 and 10 on purpose. Toxic, Ember and Monochrome have a
// name and a palette in GITD_Presets and no profile behind them, so listing
// them would offer a row that changes the colours and nothing else -- which is
// how a preset gets reported as broken rather than as absent. They go in when
// they have a profile. HasProfile() is the list that decides, and this block
// must agree with it: a row here for a preset it refuses is a row that silently
// does half of what it says.

// DarkDoom's own mode names, restored. They were briefly all labelled "Use
// the How dark dial" because all four genuinely behaved identically once the
// per-mode maths went missing; the maths is back, so the names are back.
