// THE HEATMAP.
//
// Every death drops a mark on the floor and the marks accumulate over the
// whole life of the map, so walking back through somewhere you cleared shows
// you what happened there.
//
// It is NOT the disturbance array that drives reactive fog. That is eight
// short-lived events held in uniforms; this is hundreds of permanent deposits
// that have to be summed, and a sum wants a bucket rather than a list. So it
// is a grid over the map's own bounding box, which is why the thousandth
// death costs exactly what the first one cost.
